   "signal": "REGULATORY TRIGGER: on 17/07/2026 the CBCG Council adopted a set of rules completing the legal, operational and TARIFF framework for instant payments, including a Decision limiting the fee on domestic instant credit transfers up to EUR 200 made via mobile or internet banking to a maximum of 5 euro-cents (same cap on the receiving side). CBCG states the previous AVERAGE fee for such payments was 32 cents - a ~6x price cut (PM Milojko Spajic used the same 'about six times cheaper' framing). CBCG estimates savings of ~EUR 1 million a year at current electronic volumes, rising to ~EUR 2.8 million a year as users migrate to electronic instant payments; longer term CBCG puts the combined SEPA + instant-payments economic benefit at ~2.3% of GDP annually. Transactions below the EUR 3,000 instant cap represent almost 80% of all transactions. Go-live was conditional on Parliament passing amendments to the Law on Payment Transactions (Zakon o platnom prometu), which was in parliamentary procedure as of 03/07/2026.",
